+# Ordinary financial IAM enrollment — source candidate, not runtime acceptance
+
+This separate Linux-only lane implements nineteen new HTTP case forecasts (thirteen
+ordinary enrollment rows plus six Accounting rows). It is
+not included in the existing accepted genuine IAM project or its 935/31/11 results.
+It references the **current Auth source candidate** explicitly, not the archived
+Auth `88e430946465a1df6238e10b815d495d43453411` project. The unchanged source preparation
+script supplies IAM `4fe6642e5674013de9a3672505aec898fdcae0ed`, original Aspire
+`01d506203763b914e237268a8746f1406423df86`, Messaging
+`559a00db0c7920a5247fdff60d4476ad23a9a501`, accepted Defaults
+`7b3099bf67d0f17e56cfdb3dcf36541304abaac2`, and CompatibilityContracts
+`78e48ffc4ee000df0510cba5e7c7a3c4c4d539d7`. Retaining its old Auth archive is not
+an assertion that old producer and current candidate are equivalent.
+
+The IAM MT8 graph runs in its own prebuilt `OrdinaryFinancialIamHost`; current
+Auth/Defaults stay in the test process. Both use real Program and RS256 validation.
+Only the external broker publisher is controlled. The dedicated Auth consumer's
+canonical HTTPS route is forwarded to exact owned loopback IAM HTTP; the response
+is not fabricated. TLS/certificate and broker-delivery qualification are excluded.
+
+## Actual implemented authority path
+
+The disposable legacy identity store holds a non-GUID employee ID. Real Auth
+`POST /auth/v1/login` validates its password and persists the refresh/session
+record; the unchanged issued subject is used as the IAM target. The independent
+IAM host inserts **no** positive principal, permission, or binding. Normal
+`POST /iam/v1/principals` generates a server GUID for the exact opaque resolver's
+lower-case `@serviceaccount.maliev.local` email. Readback verifies that GUID,
+email, type and active status. Auth/Quotation service subjects similarly come
+from real credential-first `/service/login`; separate secrets are generated.
+
+A second disposable real Auth Program issues the normal operator service token
+for the IAM audience with exactly the declared enrollment/registration API
+permissions, never `*`. This supplies test-only operator authority; it does not
+claim a deployed operator token, automatic enrollment, platform bootstrap,
+managed-workload equivalence, or live policy grants. Anonymous, check-only and
+wrong-audience enrollment callers must leave the attempted principal absent.
+
+The normal permission registration, custom-role creation, principal creation,
+finite role grants, readback and exact binding revocation use real IAM HTTP APIs.
+Each created role contains exactly one permission. Employee scope is one literal
+quotation resource. Auth/Quotation financial-read scope is global with a two-minute
+binding expiry. SQL writes are restricted to the disposable legacy identity seed;
+no positive IAM authority seed or employee-subject rewrite is used.
+
+## Mandatory immutable producer input admission
+
+`ORDINARY_FINANCIAL_ACCOUNTING_CATALOGUE_PATH` must identify the frozen Accounting
+producer payload `provisioning/iam/accounting-financial-ownership.json` from the
+source-clear 44-file packet (`2d619689fead1344a38c84f9c97097efb0206d146b77326e9d7aeb901d57a90a`).
+The code requires its exact raw SHA256
+`7ef027009178f40ec7d21645d4fb15dea39e779c4a5929edb8cde10a46074ef7` and registers it
+through `POST /iam/v1/permissions/register` with ServiceName `legacy`.
+
+`ORDINARY_FINANCIAL_QUOTATION_CATALOGUE_PATH` is required for the original thirteen
+rows. Its exact reviewed producer is `quotation-iam-catalogue-registration-source-v2-20261008`
+receipt `b9cc1463d43a818d672a06230c6d77ee975a5369ceb5ddade1b8848673a0a84e`,
+`source/provisioning/iam/quotation-permissions.json` raw SHA256
+`7a7ff1e9122be3ff8f914390d63b447a50e25f5f03f41e75e7609eed499ed34d`.
+The fixed hash is checked against bounded bytes and the payload must declare
+`legacy.quotations.update`. Missing/mismatched input blocks execution. There is no
+constant-only catalogue fallback or direct permission INSERT.
+
+The separate six-row `OrdinaryAccounting_` collection now joins actual Accounting
+Program HTTP and immutable PostgreSQL financial rows. Build with `AccountingSourceRoot`
+pointing to exact source-clear combined49 (`cc314f03b3cee337ddd2ea40609a7c40d664a8e8177eae82b6a87b353590d0a2`)
+and provide that manifest in `ORDINARY_FINANCIAL_ACCOUNTING_SOURCE_MANIFEST`.
+Assembly metadata binds the same project/content root; all49 raw source hashes
+are checked before host allocation. This Accounting-only collection does not need
+the Quotation catalogue input. The shared default thirteen-row collection still does.
+
+Real normal Auth employee login/session plus real `/exchange/invoice-create`
+issues the delegation; Accounting's actual signature/claim verifier supplies the
+origin before scoped Admission/CreationStore transaction commits financial rows
+and an immutable receipt. The setup is not `/prepare` HTTP/source-provider proof.
+The unchanged Auth normal `IAMService` client first sends its ordinary legacy
+workload bearer to actual owned loopback IAM HTTP. That bearer has the legacy
+audience, so actual IAM returns 401. The real nonlive Auth permission handler then
+uses its existing exact signed `legacy-auth.invoice-delegation.issue` claim fallback.
+Bootstrap asserts that actual owned denial and zero unregistered transport
+attempts; it is not a positive IAM enrollment/grant proof for delegation issuance.
+Every other unregistered Auth HTTP transport is rejected before external send.
+This is separate from the successful dedicated live financial-read IAM profile.
+It never fabricates ownership JSON or positive IAM rows. Normal IAM APIs grant,
+read back and revoke finite global financial-read bindings for real normal
+Auth-issued `service:legacy-auth` and `service:legacy-quotation` subjects. Accounting's
+real named IAM client obtains a real `AccountingService` profile from normal Auth
+and performs real uncached IAM HTTP. Positive/revocation, unrelated workload with
+its own actual binding, wrong-key, genuine wrong-profile-token transport corruption,
+and wrong inbound audience preserve financial-row hashes; key/profile recovery
+must regain a real successful read. The unrelated test-only normal service registry
+and enrollment are adversarial proof, not production AppHost/client grants.
+Redis is disabled by supported cache configuration; no Redis/provider acceptance
+is asserted. TLS is substituted with owned loopback HTTP; external broker remains
+controlled. Quotation orchestration, complete `/prepare` transport, operator CLI
+and optional AppHost whole-business graph remain separate/unqualified.
+
+## Resource and validation obligations
+
+The resource boundary is a separately adapted copy of the accepted ownership
+source, not a modification to its accepted files. Before RSA/host/container
+allocation it requires Linux MemAvailable >=4096 MiB. PostgreSQL has precreation
+512 MiB/one-CPU limits, loopback publication, tmpfs128 MiB, exact owner/run/expiry
+labels, and an actual 900-second TERM timeout around the original entrypoint.
+Startup has a two-minute caller deadline; real factory startup tasks are retained
+and joined before shutdown, keys/pools/backend release are fenced on verified
+host quiescence, and teardown attempts independent named resources with 30-second
+windows. Docker helpers preserve exact process handles and quarantine unresolved
+readers; removal verifies IDs, creation/start evidence, image/content identity,
+labels, mounts and kernel storage policy, then exact daemon absence, never volume
+deletion or broad process termination. The IAM host has a ten-minute lease,
+512 MiB managed-heap setting and one logical processor; these are **not** an
+OS-wide memory/CPU cap claim. Its exact handle, readers, input and exit task are
+retained until quiescent. SDK/host OS caps and external exact recovery still need
+the coordinator's independently reviewed finite native runner before execution.
+Faulted or interrupted `WebApplicationFactory.Services` startup does not prove the
+actual Program entrypoint has stopped. All three new factory wrappers retain a
+sticky uncertain-startup guard, independently attempt cached factory disposal, and
+quarantine dependent keys, pools and PostgreSQL even when the Services task or
+disposer settles. Only an exact finite external SDK owner proving whole-unit
+quiescence may recover that backend. No ApplicationStopped or task-completion
+event is substituted for that proof; the failed qualification stays failed.
+
+The linked accepted helper-control source remains unchanged. Its discovered
+controls must not be counted as new test passes. The thirteen ordinary rows, six Accounting HTTP rows, eleven
+V3 controlled profile rows, and all linked controls are unexecuted in this
+successor. Independent source review must precede native admission. After that,
+prepare the exact committed dependency graph and immutable producer inputs;
+build both new projects Release with zero warnings/errors, run the
+`FullyQualifiedName~OrdinaryFinancial_|FullyQualifiedName~OrdinaryAccounting_`
+nineteen-row focus and the full new project (39 forecasts: nineteen new rows plus
+twenty linked retained controls), relevant existing suites and raw
+coverage floors, format checks, and retain exact source bindings/TRX/cleanup
+receipts. Do not execute these commands while the 4096 MiB floor is failing.
+
+No live IAM grants, database/provider writes, credentials, deployment, commit or
+publication are part of this source-authoring phase. Actual task resources at
+packet creation: zero workers, containers, listeners and helpers.
+
+The eleven V3 new profile rows are in the existing AuthService project, not this
+project. Its selected LoginResponseWrongTrust method has29 forecasts: eleven new
+and eighteen retained. Together the two focused runs have48 forecasts, of which
+thirty are new candidate tuples and eighteen are retained. The normal Auth suite
+has946 forecasts (935 retained plus eleven new); existing genuine31 remains
+unchanged. Qualification must join each named TRX tuple, not treat30 as one
+project's execution count or attribute old hosted935/31/11 passes to this source.
