@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+# Financial IAM consumer recovery — source candidate only
+
+Base: Auth `85a00d4bb54cf95199ee67dfd97d2b168233ff68`.
+
+This successor imports the four production and two controlled-HTTP regression
+changes from `auth-financial-iam-consumer-source-v2-out-of-process-20261007`.
+The normal hosted dependency graph explicitly selects accepted Defaults
+`7b3099bf67d0f17e56cfdb3dcf36541304abaac2`, which supplies the separate IAM
+provider. The existing isolated genuine IAM graph already selects that revision.
+No other dependency pin, accepted genuine test, enrollment, or permission catalogue
+is changed here. No deployment or live grant is authorized by this document.
+
+## Token boundaries
+
+The dedicated quotation live-authority client uses the server-owned AuthService
+IAM profile issued by the real `/auth/v1/service/iam-login` endpoint. Its audience
+must differ from the ordinary legacy audience. Exact admission claims, issuer,
+RS256 signature, bounded lifetime, canonical origin, live-check credential,
+uncached scoped employee decision, and independent token cache remain required.
+The ordinary service token is not a fallback for this dedicated IAM client.
+
+Accounting and employee/customer profile clients retain the ordinary legacy
+provider, `service:legacy-auth` subject, and exact configured permissions. Only the
+Accounting financial-read literal is corrected to the producer's existing
+`legacy.accounting-financial-ownership.read` contract. Employee identity IDs,
+session behavior, database schema, and profile wire formats are unchanged.
+
+## Separate ordinary-enrollment financial qualification lane — source implementation
+
+Do not alter the accepted synthetic `join.resource.read` tests or their UUID seed.
+Their 935 normal / 31 dedicated / 11 focused hosted observations do not prove the
+financial business graph. The old exported five-row companion directly inserts
+a UUID principal/binding and is not imported or discovered by this successor.
+
+A separately implemented, independently reviewed lane must bind exact source revisions
+for each boundary it exercises. Whole-business composition additionally needs
+Quotation and AppHost/operator bindings; their separate pending acceptance does not
+invalidate the scoped Accounting-only source lane.
+Keep the original IAM/Aspire MassTransit8 graph out of the Defaults MassTransit9
+process. Reuse qualified lifecycle code only with explicit ownership contracts;
+do not invent new fixture APIs or weaken the 4096 MiB admission floor.
+
